Purpose: Delete the in-binary update and upgrade feature (Plan 0004). The opencode upgrade command, the TUI update dialog, slash command and home-screen notification, the periodic background version check, the /global/upgrade server endpoint and the installation update events, the Installation service's latest/upgrade/upgradeMajor/isUpdate functions, and the autoupdate configuration field with its two environment flags are all removed. Installation.method(), the Method type, and opencode uninstall are unchanged: they are not update surface. Upstream tests that covered only the deleted surface are removed or trimmed inside this patch.
Upstream files: packages/opencode/src/index.ts, packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/upgrade.ts, packages/opencode/src/cli/upgrade.ts, packages/opencode/src/cli/cmd/tui.ts, packages/opencode/src/cli/tui/worker.ts, packages/opencode/src/installation/index.ts, packages/opencode/src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/groups/global.ts, packages/opencode/src/server/routes/instance/httpapi/handlers/global.ts, packages/tui/src/app.tsx, packages/tui/src/index.tsx, packages/tui/src/routes/home.tsx, packages/tui/src/component/dialog-update.tsx, packages/tui/src/context/update-notification.tsx, packages/schema/src/installation-event.ts, packages/schema/src/event-manifest.ts, packages/core/src/flag/flag.ts, packages/core/src/config.ts, packages/core/src/v1/config/config.ts, packages/core/src/v1/config/migrate.ts, packages/core/src/plugin/skill/customize-opencode.md, packages/opencode/test/installation/installation.test.ts, packages/opencode/test/cli/upgrade.test.ts, packages/opencode/test/server/httpapi-global.test.ts, packages/opencode/test/config/config.test.ts, packages/core/test/config/config.test.ts, packages/tui/test/component/dialog-update.test.ts
Rebase note: The coupling points are the TUI application component (provider and slash command), the CLI tui command (updater factory), and the global API group (endpoint). If upstream restructures the installation service, keep only method() and the Method type. The event manifest loses the two installation event definitions with the feature.

